====================================================================================================
op                   mode       JAX fp16     JAX bf16     JAX fp32     JAX fp64   NumPy fp16   NumPy fp32   NumPy fp64
add                  eager           0.5          0.5          0.5          0.0          0.5          0.5          0.0
add                  jit             0.5          0.5          0.5          0.0          nan          nan          nan
exp                  eager           0.5          0.5          0.9          1.0          0.5          2.2          0.0
exp                  jit             0.5          0.5          0.9          1.0          nan          nan          nan
chain                eager           0.7          0.7          0.7          1.0          0.7          0.7          0.0
chain                jit             0.7          0.7          0.7          1.0          nan          nan          nan
matmul               eager           0.5          0.5          1.0          0.0          0.5          1.0          0.0
matmul               jit             0.5          0.5          1.0          0.0          nan          nan          nan
matmul_explicit      eager           1.2          1.2          1.2          0.0          1.2          1.2          0.0
matmul_explicit      jit             1.2          1.2          1.0          1.0          nan          nan          nan

  0 ULP means bit-identical to NumPy at that precision. A fraction of
  a ULP is just the rounding of the float64 reference down to the
  result dtype; >1 ULP on exp/cos means XLA and NumPy picked different
  approximations, which is a result about the libraries rather than an
  error in the harness. The NumPy fp64 column is 0 by construction --
  it is the reference. nan entries are combinations that were not run,
  or that failed validation outright (listed above).

